### Daybook API — the Step 2 acceptance path, in order.
### Works with the VS Code REST Client extension, or translate to curl.
### Cookies: REST Client keeps the session cookie between requests automatically.

@base = http://localhost:4000/api

### 0. Health
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "0249990001", "pin": "4726", "shopName": "Test Shop" }

### 2. Log out, then log back in
POST {{base}}/auth/logout

###
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "0249990001", "pin": "4726" }

### 3. Who am I
GET {{base}}/me

### 4. Sync three entries (first sync: since is null)
POST {{base}}/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "since": null,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "SALE", "channel": "CASH", "amountPesewas": 24000,
      "note": "Paracetamol carton",
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T16:12:04.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "SALE", "channel": "MOMO", "amountPesewas": 8500,
      "note": null,
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T15:48:00.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "EXPENSE", "channel": "CASH", "amountPesewas": 18000,
      "note": "Fuel for generator",
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T13:20:00.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    }
  ],
  "dayCloses": []
}

### 5. Send the SAME batch again — idempotent, expect no duplicates,
###    rejected stays empty, and the read-back below still shows 3 entries.
POST {{base}}/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "since": null,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "SALE", "channel": "CASH", "amountPesewas": 24000,
      "note": "Paracetamol carton",
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T16:12:04.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "SALE", "channel": "MOMO", "amountPesewas": 8500,
      "note": null,
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T15:48:00.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "EXPENSE", "channel": "CASH", "amountPesewas": 18000,
      "note": "Fuel for generator",
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T13:20:00.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    }
  ],
  "dayCloses": []
}

### 6. Attempt to change amountPesewas on an existing id —
###    expect rejected: [{ id: 1111..., reason: "IMMUTABLE_FIELD", fields: ["amountPesewas"] }]
###    and the stored row unchanged on read-back.
POST {{base}}/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "since": null,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
      "businessDate": "2026-07-25",
      "kind": "SALE", "channel": "CASH", "amountPesewas": 99000,
      "note": "Paracetamol carton",
      "createdAtDevice": "2026-07-25T16:12:04.000Z",
      "voidedAt": null, "voidReason": null
    }
  ],
  "dayCloses": []
}

### 7. Read back via a since delta (empty push). Use an old timestamp to see
###    all three entries; a recent one to see none.
POST {{base}}/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{ "since": "2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "entries": [], "dayCloses": [] }

### 8. CSV export
GET {{base}}/me/export
